  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce has obligated $3.8B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Commerce recorded 7,438 awards with an average award size of $517K, and obligations fell 7.6% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a peak of $5.2B in FY24 and a decline to $4.2B in FY25 before the current FY26 to date total of $3.8B. Information-technology related services dominate spending in FY2026 to date, led by Other Computer Related Services at $721M, Computer Systems Design Services at $580M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $402M. The Department of Commerce also obligates meaningful amounts to publishing and consulting categories, with All Other Publishers at $220M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $176M. Large single vendors capture substantial shares of Commerce contracts in FY2026 to date, with REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $132M. The top vendors list includes major defense and professional services firms such as LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $108M and BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $95.9M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce obligations rose to $5.2B in FY24 before falling to $4.2B in FY25. The Department of Commerce obligations in FY26 to date are $3.8B, which is down 7.6% year over year. The Department of Commerce completed 7,438 awards in FY26 to date with an average award size of $517K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is the Department of Commerce spending most of its contract dollars?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest NAICS category in FY2026 to date at $721M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $580M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $402M. The Department of Commerce also spends in publishing and consulting categories, including All Other Publishers at $220M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $176M."
      }
    ]
  },
